A C header and a directory below testdata that the test makes the run unable to
read. Either may name any function or variable of the tree, so every one is
retained against the first, docs/secret.h; a constant is no symbol another
compilation unit reaches by name, so it is not.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/unreadable

go 1.27.0
-- docs/secret.h --
int unread;
-- testdata/pg/PG_VERSION --
17
-- p/p.go --
package p

const Limit = 3

var spare int

func Run() {}
-- main.go --
package main

import "example.com/unreadable/p"

func main() { p.Run() }
